  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a library management system intended to efficiently organize and manage various aspects of a library's operations, including book collections, genres, and reservations. It aims to provide a structured approach to handling the library's inventory and user interactions.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe primary objective of the library management system is to streamline the management of books and genres, facilitate reservations, and maintain comprehensive records involving patrons and authors. The system should enhance the operational efficiency of the library by providing an accessible and secure way of managing its resources.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Library Administrators: Manage book inventory, author information, and genre categorizations.\n- Patrons: Search for books and make reservations.\n- Authors: Provide book details and personal information.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Book Management: Allow administrators to add, update, and delete book records, associating them with the relevant genre and author information.\n- Genre Management: Enable the categorization of books by genre, facilitating easier searching and browsing.\n- Author Management: Maintain detailed records of authors, including their personal information.\n- Patron Management: Enable the registration and management of patron information.\n- Reservation System: Allow patrons to reserve books, with system support for tracking reservation statuses and notifications.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: The system should efficiently handle an expanding number of books, genres, authors, and reservations.\n- Usability: The interface must be user-friendly, with intuitive navigation for both administrators and patrons.\n- Security: Ensure the secure handling of user information and a robust authentication system for patron and administrator access.\n- Reliability: The system should be highly reliable with consistent uptime to facilitate ongoing library operations without interruptions.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0237\nCREATE TABLE `authors` (\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `biography` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`author_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `genres` (\n  `genre_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `genre_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`genre_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `genre_name` (`genre_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `patrons` (\n  `patron_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password_hash` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`patron_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `email` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `books` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `isbn` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `publication_year` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `genre_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `available_copies` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `total_copies` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `isbn` (`isbn`),\n  KEY `genre_id` (`genre_id`),\n  KEY `author_id` (`author_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `books_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`genre_id`) REFERENCES `genres` (`genre_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `books_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `authors` (`author_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reservations` (\n  `reservation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `patron_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reservation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `notification_sent` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `pickup_deadline` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`reservation_id`),\n  KEY `patron_id` (`patron_id`),\n  KEY `book_id` (`book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `reservations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patron_id`) REFERENCES `patrons` (`patron_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `reservations_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `books` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
